I often need to run count_nonzero on boolean tensors. The current impl does not specialize for this dtype and checks !=0 again.



      pytorch/aten/src/ATen/native/TensorAdvancedIndexing.cpp


        Lines 2286 to 2288
      in
      68570fc







           Tensor count_nonzero_cuda(const Tensor& self, IntArrayRef dims){ 




             return (self != 0).sum(dims); 




           } 





Can we add a check that if the tensor is bool the comparison is skipped?
cc @msaroufim

🐛 Describe the bug
@overload
def istype(
    obj: object, allowed_types: Type[T]
) -> TypeIs[T]: ...

@overload
def istype(
    obj: object, allowed_types: Tuple[Type[Unpack[Ts]]]
) -> TypeIs[Union[Unpack[Ts]]]: ...

it should be more something like this. Currently, it is not narrowing correctly.
Everything is being overladed by the non-typeguarded iterable boolean overload which is breaking everything unfortunately.
